    "aboutPortrait": "images/APL02083-5 (1).jpg",
    "aboutHeading": "Through my Eyes",
    "aboutText": "Photography has been my way of paying closer attention to the world around me.\n\nI'm drawn to the way light shapes a scene, how composition can change the way we see something, and how a single moment can carry so much emotion. Whether I'm photographing a person, a landscape, or else, I'm looking for images that feel honest and intentional.\n\nPortraits are meaningful to me because I'm fascinated by the beauty of how light, composition, and movement can show both strength and vulnerability in humans.\n\nAt its core, my work is about finding beauty in the details that sometimes are easy to overlook and creating photographs that people want to return to enjoy more than once.",
    "printsHeading": "Selected works, on paper.",
    "printsIntro": "A number of photographs from each collection are available as fine-art prints, produced in small runs through a partner. \n\nNot every image is available as a print. When one is, you'll find a \"View Print Options\" link on that photograph's page, which will take you to Darkroom's site to place your order.",
    "printsNote": "Ordering, framing, and shipping are handled entirely by Darkroom. This site exists only to show my work.",
    "contactHeading": "Get in touch.",
    "contactIntro": "For commissions, exhibition inquiries, or general correspondence. A note here reaches me directly."
